1933-  ```console
1934-  $ just
1935-  bosh: ''
1936-  ```
1937-
1938-#### Invocation Information
1939-
1940:- `is_dependency()` - Returns the string `true` if the current recipe is being
1941-  run as a dependency of another recipe, rather than being run directly,
1942-  otherwise returns the string `false`.
1943-
1944-#### Invocation Directory
1945-
1946-- `invocation_directory()` - Retrieves the absolute path to the current
1947-  directory when `just` was invoked, before `just` changed it (chdir'd) prior
1948-  to executing commands. On Windows, `invocation_directory()` uses `cygpath` to
1949-  convert the invocation directory to a Cygwin-compatible `/`-separated path.
1950-  Use `invocation_directory_native()` to return the verbatim invocation
1951-  directory on all platforms.
1952-
1953-For example, to call `rustfmt` on files just under the "current directory"
1954-(from the user/invoker's perspective), use the following recipe:
1955-
1956-```just
1957-rustfmt:
1958-  find {{invocation_directory()}} -name \*.rs -exec rustfmt {} \;
true false
